UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Queen of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Radiance"—the high-frequency, mature phase of the fire element where the sovereign consciousness has fully integrated its creative intent into a warm, magnetic, and authoritative presence. Moving beyond the knight’s kinetic propulsion, the Queen signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Anchor," where you no longer need to "charge" toward your goals, but instead draw them to you through the sheer force of your own, aligned presence. Visually depicted as a queen seated on a throne decorated with lions and sunflowers, holding a blossoming staff, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Charisma"—the understanding that true power is the ability to hold a field of energy so vibrant, confident, and unapologetic that it inspires and organizes the reality around you without the need for force. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Integrated Leadership," where your internal drives have stabilized into a consistent, radiant "glow." When the Queen of Wands appears, your system is registering a "Maximum Magnetism" status; you are secure in your authority, and you are being invited to stop "proving" yourself through action and instead lead through the depth and truth of your being. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your self-worth. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Radiance": honoring your own inner fire, trusting the magnetism of your authentic self, and refusing to diminish your light to make others comfortable. To inhabit the Queen of Wands is to master the art of "Strategic Presence," recognizing that by simply owning your power, your history, and your creative vitality, you are performing the most potent act of sovereign leadership possible—giving others the permission to own their own, internal fires.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Queen of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Dissonance," "Magnetism-Collapse," or the catastrophic—yet instructive—failure to maintain your inner fire, leading to a state of reactive, insecure, and often performative volatility. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "being loud" or "controlling" with "having power," even as your internal operating system is experiencing a critical failure of self-trust. You are essentially "flickering in the dark," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s need for external attention and validation over the sober, unglamorous requirement to ground yourself in your own, genuine worth. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "confident leader," while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of insecurity, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of "performing confidence," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your radiance is a brittle, artificial projection. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of validation-seeking"; you are obsessively trying to force people to see you as powerful, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, internal restoration of your authority is your own, deep-seated fear that without this performative armor, you would be seen as "nothing." The reversed Queen of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of irrelevance, and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense and sit quietly in the truth of your own, unvalidated state, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these performative, status-seeking scripts, perform a brutal audit of your internal sense of value, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize your soul-integrity over your social-standing. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical self-acceptance—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "being perceived as powerful" over the vulnerability of "being actually grounded," and realizing that until you are willing to let the performance collapse and stand in the raw, unadorned reality of your own, quiet truth, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom magnetism you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 27;
